# ShellCheck configuration for the HTH Code Pack corpus.
#
# Every exclusion below is justified by a measured, structural property of the
# pack system — not by "it was noisy." Adding a code here without that evidence
# is a suppression, and the validate-hth-guide skill treats it as a failure
# disguised as a fix. Fix the code instead.
#
# Measured on the corpus at time of writing: 77 findings at -S warning across
# 49 files. The three exclusions below account for 48 of them; the remaining
# ~13 (SC2046, SC2155, SC2128, …) are genuine and are being fixed, not silenced.

# SC1083 — "This { is literal."
# 16 instances, all from the GitHub CLI's own path-template syntax:
#   gh api /orgs/{org}/…
# The braces are literal input to `gh`, not shell expansion. Unfixable without
# breaking the documented command.
disable=SC1083

# SC2034 — "Variable appears unused."
# 30 instances. Packs are excerpted: `HTH Guide Excerpt: begin/end` markers pull
# a SUBSET of the file into the guide, so a variable assigned inside one region
# and consumed outside it reads as unused to a whole-file linter. Structural to
# the pack system.
disable=SC2034

# SC1090/SC1091 — "Can't follow non-constant source."
# The mandated shared-library idiom across all 18 vendor `common.sh` files:
#   source "$(dirname "$0")/common.sh"
# The path is intentionally relative so a pack stays runnable from any checkout.
disable=SC1090
disable=SC1091

# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   SC2148 (missing shebang)  — that is a real defect; validate-packs.sh check 6.
#   SC1072/SC1073/SC1078/…    — parse errors. Files that legitimately cannot parse
#                               (documentation snippets with <placeholder> tokens)
#                               declare themselves with an in-file directive:
#                                 # HTH Pack Directive: doc-snippet — <reason>
#                               which validate-packs.sh check 7 validates in turn.
